Package: stabilitest
Title: Robustness and Fragility Analysis of Statistical Test Conclusions
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("Marius", "Ally", email = "marally@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Quantifies the stability of statistical conclusions in clinical
    trials and applied research. Integrates jackknife leave-one-out analysis,
    greedy worst-case observation removal (in the spirit of the maximum
    influence perturbation of Broderick, Giordano and Meager, 2023), and
    bootstrap reproducibility probability (Goodman, 1992) into interpretable
    component metrics and a composite robustness score. Supports two-sample
    location tests (Welch and paired t, Wilcoxon, Brunner-Munzel), two-group
    binary proportion tests (Fisher exact, chi-square, prop.test), TOST
    equivalence and non-inferiority for mean differences (Welch / paired t),
    linear model / ANCOVA terms, GLM (binomial logit) terms, and Cox
    proportional hazards terms.
